  "brief": "# California crop-worker pay by county, 2015\n\n## The story I want to tell\n\nWhich county in California pays its crop workers the most? I have 26 years of Bureau of\nLabor Statistics employment-and-wage data covering every US county, and I want the 2015\npicture for crop production across California, ranked from best-paid to worst-paid.\n\n## The output I need\n\nOne row per California county, for crop production in 2015, ranked by average annual pay,\nhighest first.\n\n| column | type | meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `year` | int | the data year |\n| `area_fips` | str | the county's FIPS area code |\n| `area_title` | str | the county's name |\n| `industry_group` | str | the industry group these figures cover |\n| `annual_avg_emplvl` | int | average employment level over the year |\n| `total_annual_wages_2015` | float | total annual wages, in 2015 dollars |\n| `avg_annual_pay_2015` | float | average annual pay, in 2015 dollars |\n\n## Files\n\n- `transformed_county.csv` - one row per year / county / industry group, already adjusted\n  for inflation to 2015 dollars. Columns as above. It covers every US county and two\n  industry groups.\n\nSource: Bureau of Labor Statistics, Quarterly Census of Employment and Wages (QCEW).",
